   "steps_unavailable": "Noun, plain verb and i-adjective are encoded. The na-adjective line of the formation field is not: it reads only 'adjetivo-na + にしても', with no statement of whether the な is kept, and both literal readings fail the substitution test on 静か. Keeping the attributive な yields *静かなにしても, ungrammatical. Dropping it yields 静かにしても, a string that parses as the て-form of 静かにする plus も ('even if you make it quiet') rather than the concessive this record teaches, so a generator would emit a well-formed sentence carrying the wrong construction. The sibling record n3-ni-shite-wa states 'sem な' explicitly and was therefore encoded; this one leaves it open.",
