   "steps_unavailable": "The noun use, which the record itself calls the most frequent, is encoded. The clause-contrast use is not: the formation field says it attaches to 'a forma do verbo, adjetivo-i, ou na+adjetivo/substantivo seguido de な ou である antes de に対して', and read literally that licenses *書くに対して, *高いに対して and *静かなに対して, all ungrammatical. Whatever element the contrast use requires between a predicate and に対して is absent from this record, so encoding a clause variant would mean inventing the missing piece rather than deriving it.",
